====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  On the forest's own observable the acceleration trigger's high-z clearing is cheap: AT1's A2 cell moves the flux power by at
  most 0.0033 at z = 3 and 0.0171 at z = 2 (k_par <= 6.5 h/Mpc) and passes L365's rule (0.0250 vs 0.10),
  while the matter power at k = 5 in the same run falls to 0.23 of LCDM.  L319's matter proxy, which AT1's A3 and
  bound price, is the wrong yardstick for a late, halo-internal clearing: the flux-to-matter response is 0.022 here
  against 1.01 for a relic.  The relic calibration in this box is weak (a 1.5 keV relic moves the flux
  only 0.0132); on it the cell reads as lighter than 1.5 keV, a LOWER bound
  because the box compresses a relic's small-scale imprint more than this carrier's intermediate-scale one.  The strict
  5.3 keV line needs a higher-resolution forest calculation to decide.

